# P7-1: Settings > Developer > Display lab. The patterns; Checker and White are Fast passes (the ghost test), Clean is the Quality pass.
# Fast: the ramp left in its Fast state (a Page push, no settle pass): the emulated panel shows the driver's ordered dither.
wait 300
tap 270 424             # launcher: Settings tile
wait 600
tap 270 748             # Developer
wait 900
tap 270 374             # Display lab (under Wireless development and Status)
wait 900
shot lab-ramp
tap 200 164             # Checker
wait 300
expect-no-quality
shot lab-checker
tap 270 164             # White: after a Fast pass over the checkerboard
wait 300
expect-no-quality
shot lab-white
tap 367 164             # Text
wait 900
shot lab-text
tap 140 880             # Clean (Quality)
wait 2500
shot lab-cleaned
tap 465 164             # Fast: the ramp as one Fast push
wait 300
expect-no-quality
wait 2500                # no settle pass comes
shot lab-fast-ramp
expect-state lab=4
tap 73 164              # Ramp, then Fast again: the upside-down ramp differs in every band, so it is pushed (Fast)
wait 2500
tap 465 164
wait 300
expect-no-quality
wait 2500
shot lab-fast-after-ramp   # the dithered ramp again (only the counters line differs from lab-fast-ramp)

